│                      🔍 Analysis of the Issue                      │
│                                                                    │
│ The core issue is that the uniqueLocation method is not present in │
│ the codebase, which is required to remove duplicate locations in   │
│ the gettext build process. The user's proposed solution involves   │
│ calling uniqueLocation in the __init__ method of the gettext       │
│ builder, but since this method is missing, the code fails to       │
│ process the locations correctly.                                   │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                  🧪 Step-by-Step Resolution Plan                   │
│                                                                    │
│           1. Identify the __init__ Method in gettext.py            │
│                                                                    │
│ We've already found the init method in sphinx/builders/gettext.py, │
│ which is the __init__ method of the gettext builder. This method   │
│ is responsible for initializing the builder and setting up the     │
│ environment.                                                       │
│                                                                    │
│             2. Determine Where uniqueLocation is Used              │
│                                                                    │
│ The uniqueLocation method is not found in the codebase, which      │
│ means it is not being used in the __init__ method or elsewhere.    │
│ This is the root cause of the duplicate locations issue.           │
│                                                                    │
│        3. Check for Alternative Methods or Helper Functions        │
│                                                                    │
│ If uniqueLocation is not present, we need to rethink the approach  │
│ to handle duplicate locations. The current approach uses a set to  │
│ deduplicate, but this is not being applied in the codebase.        │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                          🧩 Proposed Fix                           │
│                                                                    │
│ Since uniqueLocation is not present, the solution must be to       │
│ remove the duplicate locations in the __init__ method by           │
