│ No. The issue is directly tied to the absence of the               │
│ uniqueLocation method, which is not present in the codebase. The   │
│ root cause is clear, and the fix can be implemented directly in    │
│ the __init__ method of the gettext builder.                        │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                    2. Where are bug locations?                     │
│                                                                    │
│  • Location 1:                                                     │
│    File: sphinx/builders/gettext.py                                │
│    Class: I18nBuilder                                              │
│    Method: init                                                    │
│    Intended Behavior:                                              │
│    The init method should deduplicate the locations list before    │
│    assigning it to self.locations to avoid duplicate entries in    │
│    the .pot file. The current implementation does not apply this   │
│    deduplication, leading to redundant locations in the output.    │
│  • Location 2:                                                     │
│    File: sphinx/builders/gettext.py                                │
│    Class: MessageCatalogBuilder                                    │
│    Method: init                                                    │
│    Intended Behavior:                                              │
│    The init method should also deduplicate the locations list to   │
│    ensure consistency across all builders. The current             │
│    implementation does not enforce this, causing duplicate entries │
│    in the .pot file.                                               │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│              ✅ Proposed Fix (Direct Implementation)               │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is resolved by modifying the __init__ method to          │
│ deduplicate the locations list using a set:                        │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  def __init__(self, text: str, locations: List[Tuple[str, int]],   │
│  uuids: List[str]):                                                │
│      self.text = text                                              │
│      self.locations = list(set(locations))                         │
│      self.uuids = uuids                                            │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This ensures that each location is unique, preventing duplicates   │
│ in the .pot file while preserving existing functionality.          │
